WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:01.420
What’s in a name?

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:05.410
Ancient folklore and fairy tales sometimes
tell of the importance of names, that they

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:08.100
can hold the power to summon or banish.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.670
Whether you buy into the superstition or not,
you’d be unwise to ignore the power a name

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:17.020
can have, especially if you ever dare to venture
into SCP-4000.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.310
Why?

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:23.449
Use your own name too many times in this extradimensional
forest, and you may find that what walks out

00:00:23.449 --> 00:00:25.450
of it isn’t you at all.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:30.090
At least once a year, the Foundation leads
an expedition into SCP-4000, to explore this

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.689
Keter-class dimension.

00:00:31.689 --> 00:00:35.500
But if you go down to those woods today, then
you’d better follow the rules.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.510
Remember, the Foundation has implemented these
strict guidelines for your own safety, and

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:42.120
it’s in your best interest to follow them.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.350
First and foremost, when referencing anything
inside SCP-4000, be it a person, place or

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:51.390
thing, you cannot under any circumstances
use names or titles.

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:56.570
Communication is key when exploring SCP-4000,
and making use of specific descriptors will

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:59.100
deter any adverse effects on your journey.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:03.460
For example, you may want to refer to the
location of SCP-4000 as “the woods where

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.080
you need to speak carefully”, an apt description
for such a place.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.390
Of course, there’s a reason the Foundation
doesn’t provide a handy flashcard of alternative

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:15.610
descriptors for any personnel taking part
in the annual mission into SCP-4000.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:20.920
Nothing found there can be referred to with
any consistent name, so it is perhaps advisable

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:26.220
to look over a thesaurus and expand your vocabulary
before visiting SCP-4000, as you’ll need

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:30.170
to come up with a lot of different ways to
refer to the people and creatures around you.

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:34.000
But don’t worry, the Foundation will be
able to train you how to properly refer to

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.280
SCP-4000 in both written and verbal communication.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:40.880
In a similar vein, the second rule states
that no personnel member should respond to

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:43.550
their own name while in SCP-4000.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:48.060
Naturally, you and your fellow expedition
team will not be alone in the forest you find

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.060
yourselves in.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:53.640
The denizens of SCP-4000 are perpetually-mutating
creatures, some appearing to be trustworthy

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:54.800
while others are hostile.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.670
It is for personnel members’ own safety
that no consistent names or titles are used

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:01.810
to refer to each other in conversation.

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:07.500
This has been known to cause personnel returning
from SCP-4000 to experience vivid hallucinations,

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:12.970
and in some instances has led to appearances
of creatures found in SCP-4000 in our world.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:17.700
Thirdly, when interacting with the lifeforms
residing in SCP-4000, personnel are advised

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:22.200
to accept any gifts that they are offered,
but are warned to, under no circumstances,

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.510
consume anything that is given to them while
inside the forest.

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:30.450
Finally, and above all, do not divulge any
name, nickname, codename, alias, or any other

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:35.680
personal designation when interacting with
any native entities, and disregard any designator

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.700
that an inhabitant of SCP-4000 attempts to
assign to you.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:43.760
Personnel must, however, remain courteous
in the presence of any native creature of

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:48.319
SCP-4000, and treat these entities with respect
and formality.

00:02:48.319 --> 00:02:54.040
Access to SCP-4000 can only be achieved by
performing Procedure 4000-Halloway, a ritual

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:59.320
requiring a steady flame in an indoor fireplace,
fuelled by only organic kindling.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:03.959
Personnel are required to combine the powdered
bones of one male lion, one male red fox and

00:03:03.959 --> 00:03:08.709
a baleen whale, and cast these into the fire
with a personal possession holding strong

00:03:08.709 --> 00:03:11.610
sentimental value to the staff member performing
4000-Halloway.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:16.600
Next, personnel are to add three feathers
of a bird such as a raven, or crow, and must

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:20.770
respond with the correct counter phrases once
the fire begins to emit a voice.

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:24.569
If these conditions are met, and the correct
responses given, Foundation personnel will

00:03:24.569 --> 00:03:27.810
gain access to the entry point of SCP-4000.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:32.440
If any error is made during the course of
performing Procedure 4000-Halloway, then under

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:35.400
no circumstances should this ritual be repeated.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:39.080
Staff are urged to apologise for any incorrect
actions, then refrain from engaging in this

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:40.560
procedure in the future.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:44.800
Should Procedure 4000-Halloway be completed
successfully, Foundation personnel will find

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:49.569
themselves arriving in the access point to
SCP-4000, emerging from the mouth of an old

00:03:49.569 --> 00:03:51.670
well in the center of the forest.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:56.460
Exploration teams sent into SCP-4000 are advised
that this dimension does not adhere to the

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:59.239
laws of physical space that personnel will
be accustomed to.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:04.260
There is a single, confirmed-safe route that
must be used when traversing the forest of

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:09.540
SCP-4000, a dirt path leading in a circuit
both beginning and terminating at the entry

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.540
point.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:14.269
Previous attempts to map the landscape of
SCP-4000 all confirm that the only way to

00:04:14.269 --> 00:04:19.079
safely exit this dimension is to follow the
entire length of this path in one direction,

00:04:19.079 --> 00:04:21.049
until eventually returning to the well.

00:04:21.049 --> 00:04:25.470
You have been warned, any attempt to travel
back the direction you came will result in

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:28.270
a loss of contact with the rest of the expedition
team.

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:32.949
As mentioned, SCP-4000 is home to a number
of entities, often noted to be undergoing

00:04:32.949 --> 00:04:35.630
continuous and dramatic changes in form.

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:39.900
These physiological mutations appear to occur
whenever these creatures are unobserved, making

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:41.990
distinguishing between them difficult.

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:46.270
When questioned about the exact nature of
these changes, the inhabitants of SCP-4000

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:51.020
claim to have no control over them, and express
distress and dissatisfaction when said changes

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.020
occur.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.620
Guidelines have been put in place by the Foundation
regarding the interactions between personnel

00:04:55.620 --> 00:05:00.039
and creatures found in the forest, and adhering
to the rules regarding the use of consistent

00:05:00.039 --> 00:05:02.539
names and titles remains vitally important.

00:05:02.539 --> 00:05:07.080
The native creatures appear semi-humanoid,
and are reported to be highly temperamental.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:11.389
Should any staff member happen to offend one
of these natives, they may be subjected to

00:05:11.389 --> 00:05:17.199
anything from verbal assault, to acts of extreme
physical violence from the SCP-4000 resident.

00:05:17.199 --> 00:05:21.639
If any Foundation personnel further question
why there are so many rules when visiting

00:05:21.639 --> 00:05:27.309
SCP-4000, then they need look no further than
the discoveries and fate of Dr Eugene Japers,

00:05:27.309 --> 00:05:32.990
who during his initial expedition to SCP-4000
in 2005, encountered a humanoid native entity

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:34.569
whose head resembled a rabbit’s.

00:05:34.569 --> 00:05:38.909
As the pair shared a polite conversation,
the rabbit-like creature made an enquiry regarding

00:05:38.909 --> 00:05:41.729
Dr Japers’ name, asking:
“How is your name?”

00:05:41.729 --> 00:05:46.750
Keeping to the rules, Dr Japers did not divulge
any name or other form of title to the creature,

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:47.750
at this time.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:51.030
However, Japers remained courteous and polite
during this interaction.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:53.880
The rabbit responded with the following:
“Are you simple?

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.750
I'm merely asking how your name is.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:06:00.330
My name has smelt of raspberries lately, I
think - or snapdragons, perhaps.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.569
It's so hard to tell these days, but one makes
an effort.”

00:06:02.569 --> 00:06:07.210
In his reply, Dr Japers made reference to
his own name as having ‘tasted rather tart

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:10.889
as of late’, before concluding the conversation
with the rabbit entity.

00:06:10.889 --> 00:06:15.880
Upon returning to the SCP-4000 forest three
years later, Dr Japers was met with the same

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:18.789
creature, and once again engaged in conversation
with it.

00:06:18.789 --> 00:06:22.720
After briefly discussing their previous encounter,
Dr Japers was able to turn their exchange

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:26.460
towards something the rabbit had mentioned
before, about finding it difficult to describe

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:27.460
its own name.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:29.999
When asked to clarify this point, the rabbit
replied:

00:06:29.999 --> 00:06:34.599
“I can only assume it's because of how long
we've been apart - my name and I, that is.

00:06:34.599 --> 00:06:37.199
It was a good name, a proud name, I'm fairly
sure.

00:06:37.199 --> 00:06:41.289
By this point, though, it's probably decayed
from its former grandeur, if it even still

00:06:41.289 --> 00:06:42.839
exists.”

00:06:42.839 --> 00:06:46.500
After this mention of its relationship with
its own name, it should be noted that the

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:49.650
rabbit referred to Dr Japers by the title
‘fellow scholar’.

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:54.869
The third and final encounter between Dr Japers
and this entity came in 2013, after the doctor

00:06:54.869 --> 00:06:58.939
was sent into SCP-4000 with instructions to
conduct a more thorough interview with the

00:06:58.939 --> 00:06:59.939
subject.

00:06:59.939 --> 00:07:04.569
It was during their third conversation that
the rabbit-man revealed details of a long-forgotten

00:07:04.569 --> 00:07:07.999
war between human beings and the residents
of SCP-4000.

00:07:07.999 --> 00:07:11.899
Apparently these creatures, the ‘Fae’,
do not originate from the forest in which

00:07:11.899 --> 00:07:15.589
they now reside, and – according to the
rabbit-man’s claims – were born in our

00:07:15.589 --> 00:07:16.589
world.

00:07:16.589 --> 00:07:19.409
“Much as it grieves me to say it, we were
betrayed,” the rabbit explained.

00:07:19.409 --> 00:07:23.159
“We had fought side-by-side, you know, in
the war against that factory.

00:07:23.159 --> 00:07:25.909
We had done nothing but help them, and what
did they do?

00:07:25.909 --> 00:07:26.909
They destroyed us.

00:07:26.909 --> 00:07:29.899
They took so many of our lives, and all of
our names.

00:07:29.899 --> 00:07:32.649
Some of us fled here when the war was just
beginning, but not many.

00:07:32.649 --> 00:07:33.649
Not many.

00:07:33.649 --> 00:07:34.919
Still, though, I don't hate them.”

00:07:34.919 --> 00:07:39.300
It has been assumed by some that the Foundation
was directly involved in whatever may have

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:43.900
wiped out the Fae, causing them to either
retreat or be banished to the forest of SCP-4000.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:48.459
An additional assumption has been made that
whatever weapons were used on these creatures

00:07:48.459 --> 00:07:52.819
is directly responsible for their constantly-shifting
state, rendering them without their own names

00:07:52.819 --> 00:07:54.210
or identities.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:57.580
Whatever the case may be, it was during their
conversation that Dr Japers, in reference

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:01.870
to their second encounter, referred to himself
as a ‘fellow scholar’ to the rabbit, in

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:03.689
order to coax information from him.

00:08:03.689 --> 00:08:07.539
However, in doing so, the doctor had unwittingly
accepted the title that the native entity

00:08:07.539 --> 00:08:08.539
had given him.

00:08:08.539 --> 00:08:12.379
By mistakenly responding to the name ‘fellow
scholar’, the doctor had broken the rules

00:08:12.379 --> 00:08:17.349
of interacting with the creatures of SCP-4000;
an easy mistake, but a costly one.

00:08:17.349 --> 00:08:22.279
The doctor would later leave SCP-4000, traversing
the safe path back to the well.

00:08:22.279 --> 00:08:26.979
Dr Japers vanished shortly after his exit
from SCP-4000, and his whereabouts are currently

00:08:26.979 --> 00:08:27.979
unknown.

00:08:27.979 --> 00:08:31.581
The Foundation has made several attempts to
investigate his untimely disappearance, but

00:08:31.581 --> 00:08:36.090
to this day he remains missing and the fur
left on the inside of his expedition gear

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:38.080
displayed no strange properties.

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:43.220
The single goal, it would seem, of the creatures
residing in SCP-4000, is the theft of names.

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:46.980
However, this naturally extends far beyond
this dimension’s definition of identity

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:47.980
theft.

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:51.270
Through an unfortunate blunder, Dr Japers
allowed the friendly nature and demeanour

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:54.850
of the rabbit-entity to trick him into accepting
the name ‘fellow scholar’.

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:59.030
By giving Dr Japers a name, the rabbit was
free to steal, not only his name, but his

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:00.350
very identity.

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:04.050
While it is unclear how this transference
is achieved by the creatures, it is due to

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:08.590
the risk of this that the Foundation employs
such strict rules for any research team tasked

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:11.560
with travelling to the forest of SCP-4000.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:16.290
Make no mistake, names have more power than
we realize, and this is evident in few places

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:21.930
more so than SCP-4000, a pocket dimension
where ever-changing survivors of a forgotten

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:24.180
massacre exist as identities alone.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:28.460
Remember, a name is a powerful thing whichever
side of the well you find yourself on.

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:32.780
Your name binds you to who you are, but if
your name becomes someone else’s, then what

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:34.910
else of yours becomes theirs too?

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:40.330
Now go check out “SCP – 106 – The Old
Man” and “SCP – 049 – The Plague Doctor

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:44.140
Escapes” for more of the Foundation’s
journeys into the strange and unknown.

